<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Add and Subtract Matrices if Defined</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Given the matrices</p>
<p>\[ X = {@X@}, \qquad Y = {@Y@}, \]</p>
<p>\[ W = {@W@}, \qquad Z = {@Z@}. \]</p>
<p>Compute each expression. If an expression is <strong>not defined</strong>, enter the zero matrix of the first matrix's size.</p>
<div><b>(a)</b> \( X + W = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div><b>(b)</b> \( Y + Z - W = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<div><b>(c)</b> \( Y - Z = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<div><b>(d)</b> \( X - Y = \) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>
<p>Matrices can be added or subtracted only when they have the <strong>same order (size)</strong>; you then add or subtract entry by entry.</p>
<p><b>(a)</b> \(X\) and \(W\) are both \({@r1@} \times {@c1@}\), so \(X + W\) is defined:</p>
<p>\[ X + W = {@X@} + {@W@} = {@stepA_tex@} = \boxed{{@ansA@}}. \]</p>
<p><b>(b)</b> \(Y + Z\) is defined (both \({@r2@} \times {@c2@}\)) and equals \({@YpZ@}\). However, \(W\) is \({@r1@} \times {@c1@}\), so \((Y + Z) - W\) subtracts matrices of different sizes &mdash; <strong>not defined</strong>.</p>
<p><b>(c)</b> \(Y\) and \(Z\) are both \({@r2@} \times {@c2@}\), so \(Y - Z\) is defined:</p>
<p>\[ Y - Z = {@Y@} - {@Z@} = {@stepC_tex@} = \boxed{{@ansC@}}. \]</p>
<p><b>(d)</b> \(X\) is \({@r1@} \times {@c1@}\) and \(Y\) is \({@r2@} \times {@c2@}\): different sizes, so \(X - Y\) is <strong>not defined</strong>.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
